From: Kakueeen <kakueeen@example.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:48:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(trash): use GDaemonVfs to maintain metadata

gvfsd-trash is built without BACKEND_USES_GVFS, so it runs with
GIO_USE_VFS=local and the local Vfs has NULL local_file_moved/local_file_removed
hooks, leaving gvfs metadata un-rekeyed on restore and un-cleaned on empty trash.

Add -DBACKEND_USES_GVFS=1 to gvfsd-trash cflags so the daemon uses GDaemonVfs,
which registers the metadata hooks and wraps the local Vfs for path resolution.

metadata::* is preserved on trash restore and cleaned up on empty trash,
with no code duplication or extra link deps; trash backend only uses local
paths so no circular dependency.

Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gvfs/-/merge_requests/346
---
 daemon/meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/daemon/meson.build b/daemon/meson.build
index 05eda6c..b3416b2 100644
--- a/daemon/meson.build
+++ b/daemon/meson.build
@@ -191,6 +191,7 @@ cflags = [
   '-DBACKEND_HEADER=gvfsbackendtrash.h',
   '-DDEFAULT_BACKEND_TYPE=trash',
   '-DBACKEND_TYPES="trash", G_VFS_TYPE_BACKEND_TRASH,',
+  '-DBACKEND_USES_GVFS=1',
   '-DMAX_JOB_THREADS=10',
 ]
 
